**The outcome.** If any check fails (a mechanical exit, Check 2 not `0`, a high finding, a Check 6
failure) or the drift result is not `clean`, it writes no record: name the gate that did not pass
and say review runs next. Nothing is retried and nothing is deleted here. If
`{{ WTR }}/{{ config.work_docs.dir }}REVIEW-{slug}-{date}.md` already holds a real review (no
`review_kind: light-check`), it writes no record either — never overwrite a real review — and
review runs next.

Otherwise every gate passed and the drift is `result: clean`:
Write `{{ WTR }}/{{ config.work_docs.dir }}REVIEW-{slug}-{date}.md` (review's own file name) with
this frontmatter — the drift block is the one from gate 5 — and a one-line body naming the gates:

```yaml
---
type: review
review_kind: light-check
task_slug: {slug}
status: PASSED
created: {YYYY-MM-DD}
drift_verdict:
  result: clean
  scope_violations: []
  scenario_misses: []
  task_slug: {slug}
  computed_at: <ISO timestamp>
checks:
  mechanical: pass | n-a
  regression: pass
  security: pass
  spec_requirement: pass | warn | n-a
  structural: not-run
---
```

`status: PASSED` is not `APPROVED`: nothing graded the change. Under autopilot, execute's boundary
then passes over review and verify only when this record is the newest REVIEW for the slug, was
computed after the session armed, and the tree is unchanged since Check 2; otherwise review runs
next. A typed `/hm:review` or `/hm:verify` still runs in full.
